## Session Discipline

- Identify the session type at the start: building, fixing, or planning (see `session-types.md`)
- One focus per session. Note tangents for later, don't drift.
- At session end: commit all work, push to remote, leave a clear handoff note for the next session
- The principle of closing sessions cleanly is universal
- Start each day with `/daily-review` to surface your top projects before choosing what to work on

## Skills Philosophy

- Skills are reusable workflows saved as markdown files in `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (global) or `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (per-repo)
- Build a skill when a pattern repeats across 3+ sessions
- Skills should be self-contained with clear trigger conditions, steps, and examples
- Global skills live at `~/.claude/skills/`. Repo skills live at `.claude/skills/` within the repo.

## Project Structure Conventions

These patterns apply to any repo that uses a `projects/` directory:

- Plans saved to `projects/{slug}/plan.md`
- READMEs are living documents updated throughout development
- Completion reports written at project closure
- Archives directory for old material (don't delete, move)
- Decision logs for important architectural decisions
- Three documents per project: `README.md` (living), `plan.md` (point-in-time), `report.md` (closure)
